# 96. Useful Comparison — Ratio vs. Rate

Ask:

> Can the student identify when two quantities share the same unit (a ratio) versus different units (a rate)?

A student who treats every comparison the same way may struggle to recognize when unit conversion is required before a comparison is valid.

---

# 97. Useful Comparison — Setup vs. Calculation

Ask:

> Can the student set up a proportion correctly, even if a calculation mistake occurs afterward?

A correct setup with an arithmetic slip is a different instructional problem than an incorrect setup with perfect arithmetic.

---

# 98. Useful Comparison — Calculator vs. Number Sense

Ask:

> Can the student estimate a unit rate or proportion result before calculating exactly?

A student who can only produce an answer with a calculator, and cannot judge whether it is reasonable, still needs support with number sense.

