# 104. Quarter-Long Skills Reinforced This Week

Lesson 5 should continue reinforcing the larger Seminar III academic habits.

Students should practice:

## Reading Before Solving

Understand what two quantities are being compared before setting up a ratio or proportion.

## Selecting a Strategy

Decide between cross multiplication and the unit rate method based on the situation.

## Showing Enough Work to Diagnose Errors

Students should record their proportion setup, not just a final answer, so errors can be found.

## Checking

Substitute a proportion solution back into the original comparison before trusting it.

## Learning From Errors

Identify what happened and choose an appropriate response.

## Retrying

Use feedback to attempt the skill again.

